{
  "cells": [
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "# Prompt Caching and Context Caching Notebook\n\n> Hands-on Build It and Exercises."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "## Build It"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "### Step 1: Anthropic prompt caching with explicit markers"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```python"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "import anthropic"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "client = anthropic.Anthropic()"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "SYSTEM = ["
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    {"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        \"type\": \"text\","
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        \"text\": \"You are a senior Python reviewer. Follow the rubric exactly.\\n\\n\" + RUBRIC_15K_TOKENS,"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        \"cache_control\": {\"type\": \"ephemeral\"},"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    }"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "def review(code: str):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    return client.messages.create("
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        model=\"claude-opus-4-7\","
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        max_tokens=1024,"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        system=SYSTEM,"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        messages=[{\"role\": \"user\", \"content\": code}],"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    )"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "The `cache_control` marker tells Anthropic to store the block for 5 minutes. Reuse within that window hits; reuse after expires and writes again."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "**Response usage fields:**"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```python"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "response = review(code_a)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "response.usage"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "# InputTokensUsage("
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "#     input_tokens=120,"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "#     cache_creation_input_tokens=15023,   # paid at 1.25x"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "#     cache_read_input_tokens=0,"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "#     output_tokens=340,"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "# )"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "response_b = review(code_b)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "response_b.usage"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "# cache_creation_input_tokens=0"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "# cache_read_input_tokens=15023           # paid at 0.1x"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "Check both fields in CI \u2014 if `cache_read_input_tokens` stays at zero across requests, your cache keys are drifting."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "### Step 2: one-hour extended TTL"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "For long-running batch jobs, the 5-minute default expires between jobs. Set `ttl`:"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```python"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "{\"type\": \"text\", \"text\": RUBRIC, \"cache_control\": {\"type\": \"ephemeral\", \"ttl\": \"1h\"}}"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "1-hour TTL costs 2x the write premium (50% over baseline instead of 25%) but pays back fast on any batch reusing the prefix more than 5 times."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "### Step 3: OpenAI automatic caching"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "OpenAI gives you nothing to configure. Any prefix over 1,024 tokens that matches a recent request gets a 50% discount automatically."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```python"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "from openai import OpenAI"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "client = OpenAI()"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "resp = client.chat.completions.create("
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    model=\"gpt-5\","
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    messages=["
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        {\"role\": \"system\", \"content\": SYSTEM_PROMPT},   # long and stable"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        {\"role\": \"user\", \"content\": user_msg},"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    ],"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        ")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "resp.usage.prompt_tokens_details.cached_tokens  # the discounted portion"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "Same cache-friendly layout rule applies. Two things kill OpenAI's cache that don't kill Anthropic's: changing the `user` field (used as a cache key component) and reordering tools."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "### Step 4: Gemini explicit context caching"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "Gemini treats the cache as a first-class object you create and name:"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```python"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "from google import genai"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "from google.genai import types"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "client = genai.Client()"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "cache = client.caches.create("
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    model=\"gemini-3-pro\","
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    config=types.CreateCachedContentConfig("
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        display_name=\"rubric-v3\","
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        system_instruction=RUBRIC,"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        contents=[FEW_SHOT_EXAMPLES],"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        ttl=\"3600s\","
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    ),"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        ")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "resp = client.models.generate_content("
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    model=\"gemini-3-pro\","
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    contents=[\"Review this code:\\n\" + code],"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    config=types.GenerateContentConfig(cached_content=cache.name),"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        ")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "Gemini charges storage per token\u00b7hour for as long as the cache lives, and reads at ~25% of normal input rate. This is the right shape when you reuse the same giant prompt across many sessions over days."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "### Step 5: measuring hit rate in production"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "See `code/main.py` for a simulated three-provider accountant that tracks write/read/miss counts and computes blended cost per 1K requests. Gate deploys on a target hit rate \u2014 most production Anthropic setups should see >80% read fraction after warmup."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "## Exercises"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "1. **Easy.** Take a 10-turn conversation with a 5,000-token system prompt against Claude. Run it without `cache_control` and then with. Report the input-token bill for each.\n2. **Medium.** Write a test harness that, given a prompt template and a request log, computes the expected hit rate and dollar savings per provider (Anthropic 5m, Anthropic 1h, OpenAI automatic, Gemini explicit).\n3. **Hard.** Build a layout optimizer: given a prompt and a list of fields marked `stable=True/False`, rewrite the prompt to put a single cache breakpoint at the maximum cache-friendly position without losing information. Verify on a real Anthropic endpoint."
      ]
    }
  ],
